-- A lambda without parentheses is the last argument of its call (language.md
-- §12.3): its body ends at the first line at or left of the line the `λ` is
-- on, so a line there that holds an argument is one the lambda would have had
-- to be parenthesised for. unexpected_token at `close` (9:9); the call is
-- parsed on, so the second lambda is its last argument and reports nothing.
bracket with open close use url =
    with
        λ() -> open url
        close
        λconn -> use conn
